  "summary": "This experiment tested a multi-profile RNA-only model using PCA encoding and avgpool aggregation, comparing it to the single-profile baseline. The validation accuracy (0.5907) and F1 (0.5727) improved over the baseline (0.4849 and 0.4639), suggesting potential benefits from multi-profile data or aggregation. However, the exact contribution of multi-profile data versus avgpool aggregation remains uncertain without further isolation of variables."
